{
  "id": "10138_kakasu",
  "headword": "{欠|か}かす",
  "reading": "かかす",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to miss; to skip; to fail to do",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to miss; to skip; to fail to do",
      "explanation": "To fail to do something that should be done regularly. Almost always used in the negative form 欠かさない (to never miss/skip)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "10138_kakasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{祖父|そふ}は{毎日|まいにち}{散歩|さんぽ}を{欠|か}かさない。",
      "english": "My grandfather never misses his daily walk.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10138_kakasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{忙|いそが}しくても、{日課|にっか}だけは{欠|か}かさないようにしている。",
      "english": "Even when I'm busy, I make sure to never skip my daily routine.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10138_kakasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{毎朝|まいあさ}コーヒーを{欠|か}かさない。",
      "english": "I never skip my morning coffee.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE: Almost exclusively used in the negative form {欠|か}かさない or {欠|か}かさず (without fail).\n\nTRANSITIVITY: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・〜を{欠|か}かさない (to never miss ~)\n・{欠|か}かさず〜する (to do ~ without fail)\n・{一日|いちにち}も{欠|か}かさず (without missing a single day)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n・{欠|か}ける (to lack; to be missing - intransitive)\n・{欠|けっ}{席|せき}する (to be absent)",
